      "text": "Holo4 is a family of agentic foundation models developed by H Company for generalist computer-use tasks. The models interact with software environments through graphical interfaces, code execution, Model Context Protocol (MCP), and APIs, enabling autonomous execution of multi-step workflows. Released in 27B dense and 35B-A3B MoE configurations, plus a smaller Holotron4 Nano variant, they are trained via supervised and reinforcement learning on synthetic tasks from an Agentic Task Factory. Holo4 represents the emerging category of GUI-capable agents that operate existing software without custom integrations."
