    "summary": "H Company launched Holo4, a new series of agentic models designed for generalist computer-use tasks, marking a push toward autonomous software interaction. The release includes a 27B dense model and a 35B-A3B Mixture of Experts variant, both accessible via the H Models API, alongside an updated Holotron4 Nano. Built on supervised and reinforcement learning across diverse environments generated by the company's Agentic Task Factory, Holo4 operates through GUIs, code, MCP, and APIs. The models are distributed in FP16, FP8, and GGUF formats with trajectory datasets for transparency. This release reflects the industry's shift from benchmark-chasing to deploying agents in real business workflows, with H Company positioning itself alongside other labs productizing computer-use capabilities.",
